Algorithm
1. Create a dictionary with initial key-value pairs.
2. Access values using keys directly and via the get() method.
3. Add and modify items by assigning values to keys.
4. Extract structural data using keys(), values(), and items().
5. Check key existence using the in keyword.
6. Remove an element using pop().
7. Iterate through the dictionary using a loop to print all recordsstudent = {
    "name": "Ananya",
    "roll_no": 101,
    "course": "BCA",
    "marks": 85
}
print("Original Dictionary:", student)

print("Student Name:", student["name"])
print("Course (using get()):", student.get("course"))

student["marks"] = 92
student["email"] = "ananya@jain.edu"
print("After modification/addition:", student)

print("Keys:", list(student.keys()))
print("Values:", list(student.values()))
print("Items (Key-Value pairs):", list(student.items()))

if "course" in student:
    print("Key 'course' exists in the dictionary.")

removed_value = student.pop("roll_no")
print(f"Removed Roll No value: {removed_value}")
print("Dictionary after pop:", student)

print("\n--- Iterating through dictionary ---")
for key, value in student.items():
    print(f"{key}: {value}")
